---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";

// Ticket 07 gave this page a real job. There are no redirects, so every dead
// URL lands here: /projects, /palette, and two blog posts that were live and
// indexed by Google. People will keep arriving here from search for years.
//
// So it is built around who actually arrives. The first line works for anyone.
// The aside only pays off for the person who came from a deleted post, which is
// the largest group and the one with the most reason to feel cheated. Telling
// them the truth about why the post is gone is the most on-brand thing this
// site can say: the whole rewrite exists because the old posts were slop.
//
// The wordmark is the way home. Clicking a name to get to the index needs no
// explaining, and it makes this feel like a page of the site rather than an
// error screen bolted to the side of it.
//
// COPY IS AUTHORED AND IS NOT JASS'S VOICE. Placeholder, same as the intro was.
---

<Layout title="404 | jass.gg" description="nothing here">
  <main class="mx-auto w-full max-w-2xl px-6 py-16 sm:py-24">
    <a href="/" class="inline-block font-hand text-display text-accent">jass</a>

    <p class="mt-10 font-machine text-micro text-muted-foreground">404</p>
    <h1 class="mt-2 font-hand text-title">nothing here</h1>

    <p class="mt-5 text-body">whatever lived at this url doesn't anymore.</p>

    <p class="mt-4 font-hand text-accent-quiet">
      came from a blog post? those are gone. an ai wrote them and it showed. the
      replacements are mine to write.
    </p>
  </main>
</Layout>
